{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"GHSA-5cjr-mxj5-wmrx","published":"2026-07-02T20:27:23Z","modified":"2026-07-02T20:45:16.214576786Z","aliases":["CVE-2026-49289"],"summary":"SimpleSAMLphp has Possible DoS via XPath Transform","details":"## Summary\n\nThis library turned out to be vulnerable to Denial-of-Service attacks using XPath transforms. A mitigation has been put in place to restrict the number of transforms and to restrict transforms to only the transform-algorithms mentioned in the SAML 2.0 Core Specifications (and specifically refuse XPath transforms).\n\n## Impact\n\nAn attacker is able to send specially crafted messages to any entity relying on SimpleSAMLphp (or directly on this SAML2-library) to be able to perform a Denial-of-Service attack.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"simplesamlphp/saml2","ecosystem":"Packagist","purl":"pkg:composer/simplesamlphp%2Fsaml2"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"4.20.3"}]}],"versions":["4.6.9","v0.1.0","v0.1.0-alpha","v0.3.0","v0.4.0","v0.4.1","v0.4.2","v0.5.0","v0.6.0","v0.6.1","v0.6.2","v0.6.3","v0.6.4","v0.7.0","v0.7.1","v0.8.0","v0.8.1","v1.0.0","v1.1.0","v1.10","v1.10.1","v1.10.2","v1.10.3","v1.10.4","v1.10.5","v1.10.6","v1.2.0","v1.3.0","v1.3.1","v1.3.2","v1.4.0","v1.5.0","v1.5.1","v1.5.2","v1.5.3","v1.5.4","v1.6.0","v1.6.1","v1.7.0","v1.7.1","v1.7.2","v1.8","v1.8.1","v1.8.2","v1.9","v1.9.1","v1.9.2","v2.0.0","v2.0.1","v2.1","v2.2","v2.3","v2.3.1","v2.3.2","v2.3.3","v2.3.4","v2.3.5","v2.3.6","v2.3.7","v2.3.8","v2.3.9","v3.0.0","v3.0.1","v3.0.2","v3.0.3","v3.1.0","v3.1.1","v3.1.2","v3.1.3","v3.1.4","v3.1.5","v3.1.6","v3.2","v3.2.1","v3.2.2","v3.2.3","v3.2.4","v3.2.5","v3.2.6","v3.3.0","v3.3.1","v3.3.10","v3.3.11","v3.3.2","v3.3.3","v3.3.4","v3.3.5","v3.3.6","v3.3.7","v3.3.8","v3.3.9","v3.4.0","v3.4.1","v3.4.2","v3.4.3","v3.4.4","v3.4.5","v4.0.0","v4.0.1","v4.0.2","v4.0.3","v4.1.0","v4.1.1","v4.1.10","v4.1.11","v4.1.12","v4.1.2","v4.1.3","v4.1.4","v4.1.5","v4.1.6","v4.1.7","v4.1.8","v4